      "direction": "monolith_slab",
      "name": "Monolith Slab Detector",
      "form_language": "A single unbroken chamfered slab: the front face is one continuous plane broken only by a recessed display window and a flush USB door, so the product reads as a milled block rather than an assembled shell. Chamfers replace fillets on the long edges to keep the 26 mm side wall visually thin while giving the tool a crisp, premium parting line; the top face is a shallow gasketed vent deck recessed 0.6 mm so the ePTFE membrane sits below the silhouette line and cannot be picked at.",
